    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field on owners, derived from the locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table, following the same pattern the codebase already uses for `locality`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Region.java`** \u2014 Added the fixed region-to-timezone lookup (`NSW->Australia/Sydney`, `VIC->Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD->Australia/Brisbane`) as the single source of truth, plus a `timezoneForRegion(String)` helper that returns the IANA name or `null` for unmapped regions (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the owner schema (right after `locality`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the setter.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added an `addTimezone` `@AfterMapping` that sets `timezone` from `Region.timezoneForRegion(Region.regionOfCustomerCode(...))`, deriving it from the same region component that already drives `locality`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 locality `NSW`, timezone `Australia/Sydney`) now passes, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS).",
