    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe structure is clean and consistent with the surrounding codebase:\n\n- **Table + lookup live in `Region`**, the class documented as the single source of truth for region tables. `REGION_TIMEZONE` sits alongside `CITY_REGION`/`REGION_POSTCODES`, and `timezoneForRegion(String)` mirrors the existing `postcodeRange(String)` lookup idiom (same null-on-miss `Map.get` shape). Right unit, no duplication.\n- **`addTimezone` in `OwnerMapper`** follows the established `@AfterMapping default void add\u2026` pattern used by every other presentation field, and is placed immediately after `addLocality`, which it naturally builds on by reusing `Region.regionOfCustomerCode(...)` rather than re-deriving the region. A maintainer would find this the obvious place.\n- **OpenAPI `timezone`** is added next to `locality` with matching `readOnly`/`example`/description conventions.\n\nNothing is becoming a catch-all, and the logic composes cleanly out of existing region helpers.",
